Arrange a veterinary visit when flea control persists, recurs, causes pain, affects eating or drinking, or occurs with weight loss or behavior change. Seek emergency veterinary care now if a dog has trouble breathing, collapses, is unresponsive, has uncontrolled bleeding, has repeated or prolonged seizures, cannot urinate, has a swollen painful abdomen, or may have been poisoned. Call ahead during transport. Do not delay urgent care while searching online.

## Prevention

Preventive care includes regular examinations, appropriate vaccination and parasite control, balanced nutrition, safe housing, hygiene, and prompt attention to changes from normal. Because risk varies by region and lifestyle, build a prevention plan with the animal's veterinarian.

